b3e0d2fc-3a7b-56cd-aff7-52f447329d1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20600" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+18z=380 \\\\  & y+9z=190 \\\\  & z=19\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 18 & 380 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 9 & 190 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 18 & 380 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 9 & 190 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-9){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 18 & 380 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-18){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 38 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 76 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b010a518-7aa3-5b53-9a6d-ef0779ff0dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With Two Pivots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7a7b363-7743-56d8-a618-5c24be0b4f22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 + z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096002} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc558c8-8631-51ce-a5b1-9f868ba1e07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096003} {:answer/id #uuid "056a178e-3c4f-500f-a27e-79116d535e75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solut