& :={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 40 & 20 & -40\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b010a518-7aa3-5b53-9a6d-ef0779ff0dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With Two Pivots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6248ef27-5866-5c8b-b47f-40c045c98bb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329915} {:answer/id #uuid "5da527d9-ebec-5f2b-a809-ed28f20b82bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329916} {:answer/id #uuid "d624cfed-3c7d-5cfc-9396-74363c97c113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10z+1 \\\\ 1+4z \\\\ z+1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329917} {:answer/id #uuid "02baac2c-af06-5b21-a8f0-55091168680c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z+1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329918} {:answer/id #uuid "fcfc0de3-5798-5ef0-945e-82f606a677b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5z-1 \\\\ 1-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6248ef27-5866-5c8b-b47f-40c045c98bb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329915} :answer-field/id #uuid "69bb13ef-7453-5057-baad-ebbd9c03da44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "23bca3c5-322d-5c3f-a423-fb871cdd59a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74626" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z=1 \\\\ -3x-6y+6z=-3 \\\\ 2x+5y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-10z=-1 \\\\ y+4z=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation, we can remove this equation from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=10z-1 \\\\ y=1-4z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b010a518-7aa3-5b53-9a6d-ef0779ff0dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With Two Pivots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39f43632-77cc-5ba4-9ac4-cbab88c4b1bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21z-4 \\\\ 6z+1 \\\\ 2-z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315087} {:answer/id #uuid "95c2040e-e859-575a-bcb4-3d7fc2ad2e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ 6z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315088} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa46026-d33f-5caf-8874-47ea19a9eb4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ -6z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315089} {:answer/id #uuid "733a7d7f-640f-520c-be29-f95f19c73593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ 6z-1 \\\\ z-2\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315090} {:answer/id #uuid "c807ab96-a9e2-51cf-9d63-92b39b013c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21z-4 \\\\ 6z+1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfa46026-d33f-5caf-8874-47ea19a9eb4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ -6z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315089} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe8968f3-8554-5e91-a997-7ff38627d31a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56ed55f9-e5ad-5415-83c0-617a3911f202" :question/math-academy-id "q-74629" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-4x-12y+12z=-4 \\\\ 5x+16y-9z=4 \\\\ 2x+6y-6z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -12 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 16 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -12 & 12 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 16 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 16 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -21 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-21z=4 \\\\ y+6z=-1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation, we can remove this equation from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=21z+4 \\\\ y=-6z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}21z+4 \\\\ -6z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
